//! spec: fn-default-params
//! mode: run
//! xfail: a default combining a declaring-file name with `#loc` needs both scopes; see default_arg_scope

// The case a fix is most likely to get wrong. A default parameter value needs
// **two different contexts at once**: its names resolve in the declaring file
// (`tag` lives in `defaultlib`), while `#loc` must stamp the *call* site — that
// is what gives `std.testing` assertions the failing test's location, via
// codegen's `relocate_loc_default`.
//
// So neither extreme works. Resolving the whole default in the caller's scope is
// today's bug (`tag` is not visible here). Hoisting the default into a thunk
// compiled in `defaultlib` would fix the scope and silently break `#loc`, which
// would then report `defaultlib.thera` instead of the caller. The fix has to
// resolve names at the declaration while still expanding the default per call
// site.

import 'defaultlib';

fn main() -> Int {
    let a = defaultlib.caller_line();
    let b = defaultlib.caller_line();
    println('${b == a + 1}');   // expect: true
    return 0;
}
